From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: recalibrate JCPLL VCO on ETH-lane link-up only

The host-side ETH lane fails to re-lock after copper re-AN events
(link comes up for ~1 s then drops) and the recovery loop only re-runs
pcs_config about 91 s later. Recalibrating the JCPLL VCO in the pcs
link-up callback makes the ETH lane re-lock immediately on every
USXGMII link-up.

Restrict the recal to the ETH PCS: the recal forces the VCO TCLVAR to
the ETH value (0x5), while the PON lane - wired to the wan port on the
XR1710G - must keep the vendor-programmed 0x3. Forcing 0x5 on the PON
lane breaks the wan SerDes and the PPPoE dial.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -998,6 +998,21 @@
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
 	data = priv->data;
 
+	/* Prevention: the host-side ETH lane fails to re-lock after
+	 * copper re-AN events (link comes up for ~1 s then drops) and
+	 * the recovery loop only re-runs pcs_config ~91 s later.
+	 * Recalibrate the JCPLL VCO on every USXGMII link-up so the lane
+	 * re-locks immediately instead.
+	 *
+	 * ETH-lane only: the recal forces the VCO TCLVAR to the ETH value
+	 * (0x5). On the PON lane - which the XR1710G wires to the wan
+	 * port - the vendor programs 0x3, and forcing 0x5 there breaks
+	 * the wan SerDes and the PPPoE dial.
+	 */
+	if (priv->data->port_type == AIROHA_PCS_ETH &&
+	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII)
+		an7581_pcs_jcpll_recal(priv, port->index, interface);
+
 	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED &&
 	    interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII) {
 		regmap_update_bits(maps->hsgmii_rate_adp,
